## Third-party attributions

### Aerodynamic coefficients

The F-16 aerodynamic coefficients used in `aircombat_bench/envs/aircraft_model.py`
are derived from the following public-domain and open-source sources:

- **NASA Technical Paper 1538**: Nguyen, L.T., Ogburn, M.E., Gilbert, W.P.,
  Kibler, K.S., Brown, P.W., & Deal, P.L. (1979). *Simulator Study of
  Stall/Post-Stall Characteristics of a Fighter Airplane With Relaxed
  Longitudinal Static Stability*. NASA TP-1538. U.S. Government work;
  public domain.

- **Stevens, B.L., Lewis, F.L., & Johnson, E.N.** (2015). *Aircraft Control
  and Simulation*, 3rd ed. Wiley. Numerical coefficient values used (not
  textbook prose).

- **JSBSim open-source F-16 model** (https://github.com/JSBSim-Team/jsbsim),
  LGPL-2.1+. Numerical values derived from it; the JSBSim simulator itself
  is not linked or redistributed.
